{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>At evening, at the sun's coming, the appointed time of your departure from Egypt.</b> Behold three distinct times: in the evening, from the sixth hour and onward — slaughter it; and at the sun's coming — eat it; and the appointed time of your departure — you burn it; that is to say, it becomes נוֹתָר and goes out to the place of burning (Sifrei; Berakhot 9)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:17.639200009Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}